showtime-libmpv is an unofficial fork of GNOME Showtime.
It keeps Showtime's GTK4 and Libadwaita interface and replaces GStreamer with libmpv.
The original authors, credits, history and GPL-3.0-or-later license are retained.

Version 50.1.1-libmpv

Install

Download the x86_64 bundle and its .sha256 file from the Releases page of this repository, then run:

    flatpak install --user ./com.ivanbelousov.showtime-libmpv-x86_64.flatpak
    flatpak run com.ivanbelousov.showtime-libmpv

The bundle uses the Flathub remote only to fetch the GNOME 51 runtime. FFmpeg, libmpv,
libass and libplacebo are bundled, so playback does not depend on codecs installed on the host.

Build

Release bundles are currently built for x86_64. To build natively on x86_64 or ARM64,
install flatpak-builder, configure the Flathub remote, and run from the repository root:

    arch=$(flatpak --default-arch)
    app=com.ivanbelousov.showtime-libmpv
    flatpak-builder --user --arch="$arch" --install-deps-from=flathub \
      --repo="/tmp/showtime-libmpv-repo-$arch" "/tmp/showtime-libmpv-build-$arch" \
      "build-aux/flatpak/$app.json"
    flatpak build-bundle --arch="$arch" "/tmp/showtime-libmpv-repo-$arch" \
      "./$app-$arch.flatpak" "$app"

Install the local build:

    flatpak install --user "./$app-$arch.flatpak"
    flatpak run "$app"
